        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Support declared MIT skill licenses",
        "body": "Closes #1377.\n\nSupports standard MIT as a stored skill license alongside MIT-0 for publish/import/API/CLI/UI surfaces. New publishes and imports detect root package.json, LICENSE, and COPYING metadata, and the summary backfill now repairs existing latest versions whose stored license defaulted to MIT-0 despite root MIT metadata.\n\nProof:\n- Stored-license detection on head `e3176afa3ef6` reads root `package.json` and returns `declared.packageJson=MIT`, `stored.packageJson=MIT`; MIT license text detection also returns `MIT`.\n- Existing latest-version backfill with current parsed license `MIT-0` and detected root MIT metadata produces `parsed.license: \"MIT\"`.\n- Real `clawhub inspect` against a local registry response with `latestVersion.license=\"MIT\"` exits 0 and prints `License  MIT (Free to use, modify, and redistribute. Attribution required.)`.\n- SkillHeader UI render proof passed for showing stored `MIT` in archive metadata and not showing `MIT-0`.\n- GitHub Actions on the pushed head have 23 passing non-Vercel checks; the remaining Vercel check is blocked on OpenClaw Foundation team authorization.",
